 ## Changelog
+- 2026-10-17 (4): TEMPORARY Fly button in the pause menu, right of Pregen (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run; test `touch_ui::tests::fly_button_toggles_and_survives_resume`). `PointerRole::Fly` + `LayoutRects.fly` + `TouchUi.flying` (a toggle kept over pause, like `sneak`); in `step_frame` jump climbs at 8 m/s, sneak descends, otherwise hover (gravity of the frame added back before `physics::step`), no fall damage while on. ponytail: water drag still sags the hover a little. Not b1.7.3 (no flying in survival): delete with the Reset button when done.
 - 2026-10-17 (3): LoD visual fixes after the device screenshots (Pregen works there: compiled and ran). Scratch crate (rustc 1.75, real `lod.rs`): `lod::tests::*` 14 of 14 pass; the full crate still needs a build on the phone / CI. Easiest first.
     - Snow: from step 2 a snow layer was a full white cube that replaced the cell it lay on (white boxes on crowns and hills at the horizon). Now `fill` drops it at step >= 2 and turns the ground block under it into the snow block (id 80); leaves under it stay green; step 1 is still the 1/8 layer. Test `snow_is_a_thin_layer_near_and_not_a_cube_far` (fails without the change).
     - Oversized crowns: `pick` kept leaves from ONE child of eight, so every mip level doubled a crown and merged trees into boxes; now two children (logs and solids still 4). `a_mip_rounds_terrain_and_keeps_leaves` changed.
